## Resume safety (a re-dispatch may re-enter Finalize)

Finalize is **not** atomic: the driver may relaunch it after a partial run (agent error, Actions
timeout, manual cancel) that already opened the PR or bumped the version but never reached the
`git mv … done/`. So **check-before-act** — make every step idempotent:

- **PR:** if a PR for this branch already exists (`gh pr list --head <branch> --state all` → open **or**
  already merged), **reuse** it / do nothing; only `gh pr create` when none exists (never open a second).
- **Version / CHANGELOG:** if the target version is already in `app/system/config.php` with its
  `CHANGELOG-NEW.md` section, do **not** bump again — the doc-writer amends that section in place
  (Rule 4: one version bump per PR).
- **Branch doc:** the doc-writer refines the existing file in place (PR# already filled, `Status`
  already ✅, CHANGELOG section already present → it adjusts, never duplicates); re-delegating is safe.
- **ROADMAP:** apply only closures not already present.
- **Ticket archive:** if the ticket is already under `done/`, skip the `git mv`.
- **Coverage gap pass:** if a `test(<scope>): close codecov patch gaps` commit already exists on the
  branch, skip step 3 — do not run a second coverage-gap iteration.

## Stuck-breaker

If a fix-loop hits the **same** FAIL **3×**, stop and report `ESCALATE: <reason>`.

## Subagents

By exact name: `refactorer`, `verifier`, `tester`, `test-writer`, `doc-writer`. (Bugbot runs as the
GitHub-App PR review, **not** as a local subagent in the cloud — see the Sequence note above.)

## Report exactly one line

`Finalized. PR: #YYY. Version: X.Y.Z. Ticket archived to done/.` — or `ESCALATE: <reason>.`
